From 56fffa2c838adfad9f359973fe868f1216cd7193 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "nipuna.dulara" <pererannd.21@uom.lk>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 09:03:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] nr: Let NrEnergyHelper handle a gNB with more than one
 carrier

Add an InstallGnb overload that takes the bands the scenario already
built for CcBwpCreator, figures out which bandwidth part belongs to
which carrier, and wires an aggregator in automatically when there is
more than one. Add a bwpIndex argument to InstallUe too, so a UE
listener does not have to sit on bandwidth part 0. Rename the examples
to the gsoc prefix and add gsoc-nr-energy-ca-example, which sets up a
carrier-aggregated gNB and shows the per-carrier energy coming out of
it.
